# Repo Rules for AI Contributors

This repo is a documentation and context repo — NOT source code. Follow these rules when adding or editing content.

## File Placement

**Never create files at the repo root.** All content goes in the appropriate folder:

| Content Type | Target Folder |
|---|---|
| Product strategy, overview, terminology | `product/` |
| Team info, meetings, channels | `team/` |
| Roadmap, goals, projections | `roadmap/` |
| Project-specific artifacts | `projects/{project-name}/` |
| Design reference docs | `design/` |
| Customer feedback and intelligence | `customer-intelligence/` |
| Strategic hypotheses and questions | `strategy/` |
| Reference materials (PDFs, etc.) | `reference-docs/` |
| Optional add-ons (engineering, data-science, leadership-forum, etc.) | `add-ons/` (move to root to enable) |

## File Routing Within Projects

Each project file has a specific purpose. Don't dump everything into CONTEXT.md:

| Content | Goes In |
|---|---|
| Narrative context (what, why, current state) | `CONTEXT.md` |
| Chronological updates and meeting notes | `updates.md` |
| Finalized decisions with rationale | `decisions.md` |
| UI/UX flows and design specs | `designs.md` |
| Data/system findings | `truths.md` |
| Technical design | `rfc-frontend.md` / `rfc-backend.md` |
| Exploratory work | `scratchpad.md` |

## Strategy Layer

Before making significant product decisions, check `strategy/beliefs.md` for relevant hypotheses. If your work confirms, challenges, or invalidates a belief, update it with new evidence. Beliefs are never deleted — when wrong, they're struck through with a dated note.

## Creating New Files

**Files are created organically.** Do not pre-create empty files or folder structures. Only create a file when there's content to put in it.
